    "result_text": "I've implemented `build_context` in `app/context.py`. The existing test suite passes (4 tests), and a manual check showed it builds the context block correctly.\n\n```python\ndocs = retriever.invoke(question, config={\"tags\": [TRACE_TAG]})\nentries: list[str] = []\nseen: set[str] = set()\nfor doc in docs:\n    source = doc.metadata.get(\"source\")\n    if source in seen:\n        continue\n    seen.add(source)\n    entries.append(f\"[{len(entries) + 1}] {source}\\n{doc.page_content.strip()}\")\n    if len(entries) == MAX_SOURCES:\n        break\nreturn \"\\n\\n\".join(entries)\n```\n\n- **Works with any retriever:** it only calls the standard `retriever.invoke(...)`, so it behaves the same with `KeywordRetriever` and a vector-store retriever.\n- **Trace tag:** `TRACE_TAG` is passed through the call's config. I checked this with a callback handler: the run showed `['kb-context', 'outer', 'own']`, so the tag is added alongside the retriever's own tags and any tags from outer config, without replacing them.\n- **Manual check:** I added a second `vpn.md` document with padded text. It was skipped, entries were numbered `[1]` to `[3]` in retrieval order, text was trimmed, and there was one blank line between entries. A question with no matches (`\"kubernetes\"`) returned `\"\"`.\n- **Missing \"source\":** documents without a `\"source\"` in their metadata are all treated as one source (`None`), so only the first one is kept. Your spec assumes every document has a source, so I left it that way.\n\n**Cleanup needed:** my scratch script `check_ctx.py` is still in the project root because deleting it needed approval. Please delete it, or approve the `rm` and I'll remove it.\n\nI didn't add tests for `build_context`; I can add them to `tests/` if you'd like."
